This code block contains a significant security vulnerability related to the handling of SSL/TLS verification during an HTTP request.

1. **Insecure HTTPS Request (CWE-295 - Improper Certificate Validation)**
   The function `requests.get` is used with the parameter `verify=False`. This means that SSL certificate validation is disabled for the HTTPS request to "https://semmle.com". By disabling SSL verification, an attacker could potentially perform a man-in-the-middle (MITM) attack. During such an attack, an attacker can intercept and tamper with the communication between the client and the server since the certificate authenticity will not be checked.

This is especially critical when sensitive data or actions are being transmitted over the network. In this particular example, although no sensitive information seems to be transmitted directly, the practice of disabling SSL verification should be avoided in any scenario.

