To mitigate these risks, it's recommended to use more secure and modern cryptography libraries (like OpenSSL), specify larger key sizes (2048 bits or better) for improved resistance against future attacks, securely export the keys using encrypted formats (e.g., PEM with encryption), and ensure input validation mechanisms are robust and comprehensive throughout all cryptographic operations.

