- CWE-259 (Use of Hard-coded Password) - Medium Confidence, assuming passwords are not securely hashed or stored as implied by the placeholder function.
- CWE-284 (Improper Access Control) - Medium Confidence due to lack of authentication/authorization mechanisms on the `/upload` endpoint.

These vulnerabilities represent common security issues in web applications and should be addressed to mitigate potential exploits effectively.
</analysis>

