The pickle module is used for serialization/deserialization in Python and allows arbitrary code execution when unpickling data (CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data). An attacker could send a crafted payload which would lead to executing harmful commands. 

To fix these issues, user input should be properly sanitised or encoded before usage and appropriate error handling mechanisms for the base64 decoding process must exist. 
