Additionally, the code is using Jinja2 template engine which itself comes with a set of security considerations like context-sensitive attacks where an attacker can inject malicious data into your templates. It's important to note that these issues are generally more severe than SQL injection as they involve rendering arbitrary user input in templates and not just databases, hence the severity level of CWE-79 is higher than CWE-89 (SQL Injection).

But, always remember that no matter how secure your server or database security is, you should never trust user inputs. So even if this function does not present a direct risk to the system's integrity, we would still consider it as a High Confidence finding. 

