In production environments, this should ideally not be set to '0.0.0.0', which means listening on all available network interfaces including those of your local machine and potentially open up the server to remote connections from anywhere in the world. This makes it susceptible to denial-of-service attacks or other exploits if someone gains access to your server. 

<analysis>
