<analysis>
This Flask route has a potential ReDoS (Regex Denial of Service) vulnerability via the `re.search()` function. This is because Python's regular expression engine is vulnerable to certain types of denial-of-service attacks involving long strings and complex patterns that cause catastrophic backtracking, or excessive memory consumption.

The ReDoS attack occurs when a regex pattern takes exponential time to complete due to repetitive constructs within the pattern. In this case, it's with `re.search(pattern, request.args["text"])`. 

For instance, if a malicious user provides a payload like `"(?=x){20000000:}"` as 'pattern', Python will take an excessive amount of time to complete the match and potentially cause performance issues or even crash.

</analysis>

