The main problem here is the use of `lxml.etree.fromstring()` without any explicit disabling of external entities or other protective measures. This function can be vulnerable to XXE attacks if it processes untrusted XML input containing references to external entities, which could allow an attacker to read arbitrary files from the server's file system, perform SSRF (Server-Side Request Forgery) attacks, or even execute code in some cases.

The vulnerability occurs because `lxml.etree.fromstring()` by default allows external entities, and the application accepts XML input directly from user requests without any validation or sanitization.
